# Windows checkouts historically used core.autocrlf=true with no
# governing .gitattributes, so committed LF bytes could materialise as
# CRLF on checkout and break checksum-governed fixtures/generated data
# (issue #55). `eol=lf` forces LF in the working tree regardless of the
# platform or local core.autocrlf setting; the actual bytes stored in
# the repository are unaffected.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
